.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH check 1  "check " 
.SH NAME
check \- Analyse the workspace and fail (exit 1) if any finding is MAJOR or CRITICAL. The canonical CI invocation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcheck\fR [\fB\-\-ci\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Analyse the workspace and fail (exit 1) if any finding is MAJOR or CRITICAL. The canonical CI invocation
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ci\fR
Canonical CI mode (directive §30): forces JSON output regardless of `\-\-format`. Behaviour is otherwise identical — `check` already loads config, consults the baseline, and returns a deterministic exit code with no interactive prompts by default
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

